    description: "**SEVERE - tranch 03's single Severe card.**\n\n**Mechanic**: The project's primitive catalog lists `replace`, `write`, `run` as ambiguous names — short names that collide with `str.replace`, `dict.replace`, `pandas.DataFrame.replace`, etc. The catalog's `classify_with_module_hint` returns None for ambiguous names without a module hint. The taint-sink matcher, however, indexes sinks purely by `callee_name` and blindly returns the first sink when no module hint is available. When an edge has `dst=\"external:0-0:replace:unresolved\"` (no module hint — the common case for unresolved Python method calls), the matcher returns the first registered \"replace\" sink (the filesystem-write `Path.replace`), so every `str.replace` in the call graph becomes a host-filesystem-write evidence row. Two consumers of the same YAML diverge on the `ambiguous_names` semantics.\n\n**Expectation**: Both consumers of the primitive catalog honor `ambiguous_names`; in particular, the taint-sink matcher returns None (not the first sink) when the callee name is in `ambiguous_names` and no disambiguating module hint is present. Reported violations distinguish true positives from ambiguous-name false-positive cascades.\n\n**Scope**: 5,541 false-positive flow violations across 4 claims on the project's own canonical claims-doc. The same defect affects any consumer running verify-claims against any codebase whose call graph includes Python `replace`/`write`/`run` calls on non-filesystem types.\n\n**Exposure**: Any consumer following the spec's documented contract for the 5-verdict vocabulary and trusting \"violated\" as authoritative.\n\n**Consequence**: A consumer concludes the runtime CLI subcommands violate a \"do not write to arbitrary filesystem paths\" security property when they do not. The user-facing exit code (1) and message (\"4 VIOLATED\") give no signal to distinguish a true violation from an ambiguous-name cascade. This is the precise decision-corruption Tier 5 defines — a security property the contract claims to verify is silently misreported.\n\n**Source**: F46.A1 (INDEPENDENT, HIGH). Pass 46 Severe candidate confirmed.\n\nFiled via tranch 03 dogfood (passes 41-60, substrate sha256 a32c4a31..., HEAD 9a18959071). Tranch state: `~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/dogfood_tranch_03/tranch_state.json`."  # 8abe
